                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/container/v2/container">
                                <title2
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    jcr:title="Award-winning approach to development"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    type="h5"
                                    variant="h"/>
                                <text2
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>At AbbVie UK, development isn’t a one-size-fits-all journey. It’s shaped by curiosity, opportunity, and the ability to explore what matters most to each individual.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>This commitment has been recognised externally, with AbbVie UK named among the &lt;b>UK’s Best Workplaces for Development™ 2026&lt;/b>, and for colleagues, it’s the everyday experiences that bring this to life.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <separator
                                    cq:styleIds="1662756423318"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/separator/v2/separator"/>
                                <title2_copy
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    jcr:title="A journey shaped by opportunity"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    type="h5"
                                    variant="h"/>
                                <text2_copy
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>For Katie Walker, Marketing Excellence Partner, development at AbbVie has been about following her interests and being supported to act on them.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Katie began her career in communications, but it was through her work in internal communications that she became curious about the commercial side of the business. With encouragement to explore that interest, she has since moved across several areas of the UK organisation, including technology solutions, marketing and now marketing excellence.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Each move has brought new challenges, new skills and a broader perspective.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Beyond her day job, Katie has also taken on the role of Chair for the Young Minds Employee Resource Group, supporting early career professionals and graduates across AbbVie.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Through this experience, she has developed in different ways, leading a committee, presenting to senior leaders, and building a strong network across the organisation.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <separator_copy
                                    cq:styleIds="1662756423318"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/separator/v2/separator"/>
                                <quote_copy_1510540232
                                    cq:styleIds="[1000000000040,1000000000000,1000000000010]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/quote"
                                    attributionName="Katie Walker"
                                    attributionTitle="Marketing Excellence Partner"
                                    dmPresetType="imagePreset"
                                    fileReference="/content/dam/abbvie-com2/uk/images/15-Katie-Walker_BR58824.jpg"
                                    quote="I feel supported to take ownership of my development and pursue opportunities that genuinely interest me. That support makes a real difference."
                                    quoteType="regular"
                                    textSize="h0"/>
                                <text2_copy_copy
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>One standout moment for Katie was presenting the impact of Young Minds to senior leadership, an opportunity to spotlight the group’s work, elevate its members, and bring back new ideas to continue its growth.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <title2_copy_copy_1822362312
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    jcr:title="Developing through experience"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    type="h5"
                                    variant="h"/>
                                <text2_copy_copy_270460907
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>For Hammad Ayub, Associate Director, Business Excellence, development has been driven by a simple mindset: learn by doing.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Starting his career in marketing, Hammad built a strong foundation in strategy and commercial thinking. But keen to broaden his perspective, he moved into a customer-facing sales role, gaining first-hand insight into what drives performance in the field.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>That experience became invaluable when he returned to marketing, allowing him to connect strategy with real-world understanding. He continued to build on this through a move into business consulting, developing analytical skills and working closely with customers to understand performance and impact.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Rather than following a fixed path, Hammad has shaped his own journey, combining hands-on experience with formal learning and taking on opportunities beyond his core role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <quote
                                    cq:styleIds="[1000000000040,1000000000000,1000000000010]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/quote"
                                    attributionName="Hammad Ayub"
                                    attributionTitle="Associate Director, Business Excellence UK&amp;I"
                                    dmPresetType="imagePreset"
                                    fileReference="/content/dam/abbvie-com2/uk/images/Hammad Ayub.jpg"
                                    quote="Development has always been something I’ve taken personal ownership of, by seeking out opportunities to learn, stretch and build experience across different areas of the business."
                                    quoteType="regular"
                                    textSize="h0"/>
                                <text2_copy_copy_copy
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>Now in a leadership role, his focus has evolved further, supporting others to grow, while continuing to develop himself through experiences like cross-functional leadership and programmes such as Coach to Lead.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>A defining moment in his career came when leading the Sales Force Effectiveness function, where he was able to bring together insights from across his career journey to connect data, analytics and field performance.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <title2_copy_copy
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    jcr:title="Creating space to grow"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    type="h5"
                                    variant="h"/>
                                <text2_copy_copy_copy_721582897
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>Katie and Hammad’s experiences are just two examples of what development can look like at AbbVie UK.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>It’s not only about formal programmes, but also about creating an environment where people feel encouraged to explore, take on new challenges, and grow in ways that are meaningful to them.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <quote_copy
                                    cq:styleIds="[1000000000040,1000000000000,1000000000010]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/quote"
                                    attributionName="Anna Oliver"
                                    attributionTitle="UK HR Director"
                                    dmPresetType="imagePreset"
                                    fileReference="/content/dam/abbvie-com2/uk/images/Anna Oliver.jpg"
                                    quote="Creating an environment where people feel empowered to learn and grow, not just for our teams, but for the patients we serve."
                                    quoteType="regular"
                                    textSize="h0"/>
                                <text2_copy_copy_copy_2102413692
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>Because when our people grow and thrive, so does the impact we can have, for each other, and for patients.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                            </container4>
                        </parsys>
                        <par_13
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="wcm/foundation/components/parsys">
                            <container5
                                cq:styleIds="[1653545847150,1653242825678,1653545835982]"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/container/v2/container"/>
                        </par_13>
                        <par_12
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="wcm/foundation/components/parsys">
                            <title2_copy_copy_cop
                                cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-22T12:06:46.010-04:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                jcr:title="Six Tips When Writing Your CV"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                langAttribute="none"
                                type="h4"
                                variant="h"/>
                            <text2_copy_copy_copy
                                cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-22T12:06:53.874-04:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                langAttribute="none"
                                text="&lt;p>Before you start updating your CV, it's worth understanding what graduate employers are actually looking for.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>At AbbVie, we're interested in more than qualifications and grades alone. We want to understand how you approach challenges, work with others and continue learning.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Whether your experience comes from university, part-time work, volunteering, placements or extracurricular activities, your CV should help employers see those qualities in action.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Here are some useful tips to help you structure an effective CV:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                            <accordion_copy_copy
                                cq:styleIds="[1]"
                                jcr:created="{Date}2026-03-30T14:21:45.736-04:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="BENNENX4"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-20T10:47:08.706-04:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/accordion/v2/accordion"
                                singleExpansion="false">
                                <item_1784200234985
                                    cq:panelTitle="1. Get the Basics Right"
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-22T12:08:21.047-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>Your CV is often your first opportunity to make an impression, and employers make that judgement quickly. Therefore getting the basics right, matters.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>A typical CV for an entry level role will look like:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Personal profile&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Your education, including:&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Institution, qualification, grade (if relevant) and dates attended)&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Any relevant modules, research projects, dissertations, industry-related coursework. Professional certifications, online learning, and additional qualifications should also be included here.&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Relevant work experience&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Other basics to consider when you're writing include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Keep your CV to 1–2 pages&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Focus your experience to those have relevance to the role you’re applying for, not everything you have ever done&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Use a clean, professional format with a clear font such as Arial or Calibri (11–12pt)&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Include your name, professional email address, contact number and your LinkedIn profile&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Many organisations use Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), so tailoring your CV can make a significant difference&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <text
                                    cq:panelTitle="2. Start with a Strong Personal Profile"
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678]"
                                    jcr:created="{Date}2026-07-16T06:48:18.413-04:00"
                                    jcr:createdBy="vickekx"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T06:51:37.090-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>Your personal profile is one of the first things recruiters will read. Keep it short, specific and relevant to the role you're applying for.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>The best graduate CV profiles answer three questions:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Who are you?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>What can you bring?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>What are you looking for?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Avoid: &lt;/b>Hardworking graduate seeking opportunities.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Try this instead: &lt;/b>Curious Life Sciences graduate with experience delivering research projects and collaborating across diverse teams. Interested in healthcare innovation and using data-driven insights to improve outcomes for patients.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <item_1784198815639
                                    cq:panelTitle="3. Prove your Skills through your Experience (which doesn't have to be a job)"
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-22T12:10:26.753-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>Many students worry they don't have enough experience. But experience can come from:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;i>University projects; Part-time jobs; Placements; Internships; Volunteering; Student societies; Research projects; Personal projects.&lt;/i>&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>It is how you take these experiences and show your learnings that the strongest CVs demonstrate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>When thinking about writing these, recruiters don't just want to know what you did. They want to know:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>What challenge you faced&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>What you contributed&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>What happened as a result&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Avoid: &lt;/b>Worked on a university group project.&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;b>Try this instead: &lt;/b>Collaborated with a team of five to research and present recommendations on a healthcare industry challenge, helping achieve a first-class project outcome.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>This shows collaboration, communication, analytical thinking and impact in a single sentence.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>This can also be applied to specific key words or job requirements:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Avoid&lt;/b>&lt;span>: Excellent communicator.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Try this instead:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>Presented research findings to an audience of 40 students, translating complex information into clear recommendations.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Avoid:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>Strong teamwork skills.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Try this instead:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>Worked across a multidisciplinary team to plan and deliver a student fundraising event attended by more than 200 people.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Specific examples make your CV more credible and memorable.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <item_1784198851353
                                    cq:panelTitle="4. Tailor Your CV To Every Application"
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T07:47:02.784-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>One of the biggest mistakes candidates make is sending exactly the same CV to every employer.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Before applying, carefully review:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>The job description&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Essential skills&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Desired behaviours&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Industry-specific language&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Then look at your own experiences and ask:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;i>&lt;b>Which examples best demonstrate what this employer is looking for?&lt;/b>&lt;/i>&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>A tailored CV is more likely to stand out than a generic one.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <item_1784198864750
                                    cq:panelTitle="5. Use AI, but read this first"
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T07:03:15.247-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>AI can be a useful tool for improving structure, grammar and clarity. But it shouldn't replace your own experiences and personality.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>A common mistake is creating a CV that sounds polished but generic.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Before submitting your application, ask:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Does this sound like me?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Could anybody have written this?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Have I included specific examples?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Have I tailored it to the role?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>If your CV could be sent to any employer without changing a word, it's probably not tailored enough.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <item_1784208464557
                                    cq:panelTitle="6. Common CV Mistakes (and what to check before you apply)"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T09:35:30.165-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    langAttribute="none"
                                    text="&lt;p>Before hitting submit, ask yourself:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Is my CV clear and easy to read?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Have I included relevant examples?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Am I showing achievements rather than listing responsibilities?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Have I tailored my CV for this role?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>&amp;nbsp;Have I demonstrated skills with evidence?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Does the application genuinely sound like me?&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>If not, it probably needs some tweaks before you hit submit.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                            </accordion_copy_copy>
                            <title2_copy_copy_cop_2007076719
                                cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T07:04:36.423-04:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                jcr:title="What AbbVie looks for in Early Talent Applications"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                langAttribute="none"
                                type="h5"
                                variant="h"/>
                            <text_copy
                                cq:styleIds="[1659545825678]"
                                jcr:created="{Date}2026-07-16T07:04:52.824-04:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T07:05:37.538-04:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                langAttribute="none"
                                text="&lt;p>When reviewing applications for our Early Talent programme, we're interested in candidates who demonstrate:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Curiosity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>People who ask questions, seek opportunities to learn and are excited by new challenges.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Collaboration:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>People who work well with others and understand that great ideas rarely happen alone.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Learning Agility:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>People who are open to feedback and comfortable stepping outside their comfort zone.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Problem Solving:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>People who can identify challenges and think creatively about solutions.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Impact:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b>People who can explain the difference they've made, whether that's through a project, volunteer role, placement or part-time job.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>You don't need years of experience to demonstrate these qualities. What matters is how you tell your story.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                            <title2_copy_copy_cop_1651046544
                                cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T09:27:08.202-04:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                jcr:title="Final Checklist"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                langAttribute="none"
                                type="h5"
                                variant="h"/>
                            <text_1941862737_copy
                                cq:styleIds="[1659545825678]"
                                jcr:created="{Date}2026-07-16T09:30:36.592-04:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-07-16T09:30:53.447-04:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="vickekx"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                langAttribute="none"
                                text="&lt;p>There is no such thing as the perfect graduate CV. The strongest CVs aren't packed with experience. They're clear, relevant and help employers understand your potential.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>Focus on showing how you've learned, contributed, collaborated and grown.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>Because that's what employers are really looking for.&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
